@SimpleResilientPaymentScenario.api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5111

### 1) Create a payment
POST {{SimpleResilientPaymentScenario.api_HostAddress}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-10001",
  "customerId": 123,
  "amount": 500000
}

### 2) Duplicate OrderId (same body)
POST {{SimpleResilientPaymentScenario.api_HostAddress}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-10001",
  "customerId": 123,
  "amount": 500000
}

### 3) Another payment with a new OrderId
POST {{SimpleResilientPaymentScenario.api_HostAddress}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-10002",
  "customerId": 456,
  "amount": 750000
}

### 4) Same OrderId, different amount (expect 409 conflict)
POST {{SimpleResilientPaymentScenario.api_HostAddress}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-10001",
  "customerId": 123,
  "amount": 999999
}